// @PLN130 probe 19 — SECRET COPY: binding a stdlib call's result.
//
// Taken from the corpus survey rather than invented: `InterpCallReturn fn n_main copies
// File` was the second most common uncovered family across tests/scripts (107 hits).
// `f = file(path)` deep-copies the whole `File` — including a reallocated `path` text —
// into a store the binding owns.
//
// Pairs with probe 15: the same `file()` callee copies here, while a user-defined
// `make()` returning a struct literal does NOT (probe 15 measures zero copies).  The
// difference is in the CALLEE's return, not the call site — @PLN130 Q5.
//
// Guard: InterpCallReturn / NativeCallReturn on `f`.

fn main() {
  f = file("/etc/hostname");
  n = 0;
  if f.format != Format.NotExists {
    n = n + 1;
  }
  assert(n == 1 || n == 0, "19 n {n} want 1 or 0");
  println("probe 19 PASSED — the File bind deep-copied, reported by nothing");
}
